The one-line edit that isolates the dp4a inline assembly, against llama.cpp b86d2f075.

It renames the condition of one branch of ggml_cuda_dp4a to a macro that nothing defines, so the
generic C byte loop is compiled while every other reader of RDNA1 in the translation unit still
sees the macro. It is a measurement instrument, not a proposed change: it is applied on top of
hip-rdna1-gfx1013.diff (evidence/m16/gfx1013-dp4a-2026-10-09), so RDNA1 is defined for gfx1013
and only the assembly is out of the way.

